<h2>4. OPTION 2: Amazon ECS on EC2 with GPU (AEX model-type = "huggingface")</h2>
<h3>How It Works</h3>
<p>Model artifacts stored in Amazon S3 are pulled to an ECS worker node and loaded into GPU memory for inference.</p>
<h3>Feasibility Assessment</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Current AEX / AWS Limit</th><th>Gemma 4 31B Needs</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Worker Ephemeral Storage</td><td>20 GiB (ECS Fargate default)</td><td>65+ GB</td><td class="fail">FAILS</td></tr>
<tr><td>ECR Image Layer Size</td><td>52 GB max per layer (AWS hard limit)</td><td>65 GB model</td><td class="fail">FAILS</td></tr>
<tr><td>GPU Support</td><td>ECS Fargate = No GPU; ECS on EC2 = GPU possible</td><td>71 GB VRAM (FP16)</td><td class="fail">FAILS on Fargate</td></tr>
<tr><td>S3 Download Time</td><td>Unknown timeout threshold</td><td>~5-10 min for 65 GB</td><td class="warn">RISK</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cold Start</td><td>Unknown health check timeout</td><td>2-5 min model loading</td><td class="warn">RISK</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Problems Blocking This Path</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Problem</th><th>Detail</th><th>Severity</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td class="fail">ECS Fargate ephemeral storage = 20 GiB</td><td>Model is 65 GB. Cannot fit. Max Fargate storage is 200 GiB but must be explicitly configured.</td><td>CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td class="fail">ECR image layer limit = 52 GB</td><td>Cannot bake the 65 GB model into the container image (AWS hard limit).</td><td>CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td class="fail">ECS Fargate has no GPU</td><td>Fargate does not support GPUs. Must use ECS on EC2 with GPU instances instead.</td><td>CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td class="fail">No JFrog to S3 transfer</td><td>No automated mechanism to move 65 GB from Artifactory to S3.</td><td>CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td class="warn">No tensor parallelism support</td><td>Cannot configure multi-GPU inference (TP=2, TP=4).</td><td>HIGH</td></tr>
</table>

